# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the .gitignore from segment 4 of the session, as a real working file.
# The comments are for the students, not for you.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Environments: commit the RECIPE, never the SANDBOX --------------------
.venv/
venv/
renv/library/
renv/staging/
renv/python/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/sandbox/
renv/lock/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOTE: renv.lock, .Rprofile, renv/activate.R and renv/settings.json are the
# RECIPE — commit them. Only the directories above are the sandbox.

# --- Files that can contain patient data without looking like it -----------
# .RData is a binary blob of whatever was in your R session. If patient data was
# loaded, it is in there, and no code reviewer will ever open it to find out.
.RData
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
# Python's equivalents: pickled and cached dataframes.
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.parquet
*.feather

# --- R / RStudio metadata --------------------------------------------------
# Per-user editor state and cached credentials. None of this describes the
# analysis, all of it differs between machines, and .httr-oauth is a live token.
.Rproj.user/
.Ruserdata/
.httr-oauth
*.Rcheck/
*.Rproj.bak

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.Renviron
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
secrets.yaml

# --- Data ------------------------------------------------------------------
# In real work, data lives OUTSIDE the repo and the repo stores a path to it.
# data/labs.csv is committed here as an exception because it is synthetic and
# this repo has to be clonable in one step — see data/README.md.
# Uncomment the next line for any project with real data:
# data/
*.xlsx
*.dta
*.sav

# --- Notebook / knit output ------------------------------------------------
# Rendered output is a build artifact: regenerate it, don't commit it. Knitting
# 01_explore.Rmd writes 01_explore.html (and sometimes an _files/ folder) right
# next to the source, and it WILL show up in git status if you don't ignore it.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.html
*_files/
*.nb.html

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/settings.json
